course: dictionary
lesson: 3532
title: Feathery: two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as 1) and 2), and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Feathery» has two meanings: covered with feathers, and light, soft or delicate, like a feather.
explain: «Fish take oxygen from water with gills, thin feathery parts full of blood vessels.» The gills are not covered with feathers. Here feathery describes their thin, delicate shape, so it uses the second meaning.
explain: «Feathery clouds» also uses the second meaning. The clouds are not made of feathers. They look soft, light and wispy. To check, swap in «light and soft». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Feathery means covered with feathers, as birds are.
fact: Feathery also means light, soft or delicate, like a feather.
fact: «Feathery leaves» and «feathery clouds» use the second meaning.
fact: «Feathery touch» means a very light, gentle touch.
fact: Feathery is an adjective. Its comparative forms are featherier and featheriest.
exercise: In «feathery clouds», what does feathery mean? | Hard and cold | Covered with feathers | Dark and heavy | * Light and soft, like a feather
exercise: «Birds have feathery bodies.» What does feathery mean here? | Shiny and smooth | Light and soft, like a cloud | Wet and cold | * Covered with feathers
exercise: Which swap keeps the meaning of «feathery leaves»? | Loud leaves | Heavy, dark leaves | * Soft, fine leaves | Leaves with feet
test: «The axolotl keeps its feathery gills on its head.» Which meaning of feathery fits best? | Heavy and rough | Covered with feathers | * Thin and delicate, like a feather | Bright and shiny
test: Which sentence uses feathery in the second meaning? | * «The fern had feathery fronds.» | «The bird preened its feathery wings.» | «The chicken laid an egg.» | «The owl hooted at night.»
exam: Which is the best meaning of feathery in «The snow fell in feathery flakes»? | Covered with feathers | Hard, sharp and cold | Dark and wet | * Light, soft and delicate, like a feather
